6. Pou'ers nnd functions of the ICT Child Protcction Advisory Boa.rd for thepurposes of this Act.- Without prejudice to the blsiness allocated to the Division corcerned, thefollowing shall be porvers and functions of the ICT Child Protection Advisory Board for the'purposes of this Act. narnely:-
(a) to analyze the performance of ZARRA, to evaluate the elfectiveness of ZARRAfunctions arrd to take actions to continually improve the performance ofZARRA;and
(b) to provide governance and oversight in order to ensure that all actions relating toZARRA thar are initiated, from registration of FIR to safe recovery of ch ld andreferral fbr rchabilitation of a recovered child, are perfonned efficiently,
7. Coordination between ZARRA and Local Police Stations. ( I ) 1'he policestation wh(:re a case of missing or abducted child is reported shall, immediately anrl not latcrthan two hours after thc complaint is lodged, through any available means of comnrunicationcall, fax, electronic email or ZARRA mobile application, inform the ZARRA of the missingchild incident and keep providing latesl status of the case and all available details. Tle missirrgor abducted child database shall be shared on online database, maintained by the ZARRA offlrcr:il accordance with the prescribed rules. The police officer shall ensure that the requireclinformation in Schedule A to this Act, is made part of the complaint.(2) l-he ZARRA shall on receipt of information under sub-section (l) take an immediattaction and launch, u,ith the help of local police, the investigation, search. rescue, recovery anrlrehabilitation operations.
(3) In case Z.q.RRA office receives a direct complaint ol a missing or abducted child, itshall coordirrate irnmediately with the local police station and other ZARRA offices to r:nsure allactions relating to .ZARRA are initiated. This includes registering of a complaint at tht'concemed police statron on behalfofthe complainanl.
PART III
